IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-79, TARGETED: the Arbitration Law, 5728-1968 ("the Law"; the English title is a working translation of the Hebrew title the first page of Sefer HaChukim 535 prints). Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records two items as typed values, and tests them. I1: section 38 of the Law cites section 19(b) of the Courts Law, 5717-1957, and section 8(b) and (d) of the Registrars Ordinance, 1936, by name and number, and later official pages print other numbers beside those two. I2: SH 2760 (28.11.2018) prints a replacement of the definition "the court" in section 1, and prints three sections, none of which names section 38.
-- SEAT: a party to a proceeding in which the court makes a decision under the Law, or in which a registrar does, who wants to appeal it. A row of references asks that person no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: an instrument as its footer prints it, a section as the page prints it (its margin note, its bracketed reference, its lettered subsections), a definition as printed, an instruction of an amending instrument, a citation of an enactment, a row of a comparison table and the table the row types, an item with its two limbs, and the questions asked of them. No reference is stated here; they are in ab79-cross-references.l4.
--
-- Each item is recorded with two limbs, as in the other targeted rows:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument read.
-- The row says what the pages print. A comparison table is typed as the rows the deposited bands print, each row as a pair (the number printed under the heading for the previous section, the number printed under the heading for the new section), and the row says nothing about what a table means.
--
-- LATIN LETTERS. The Hebrew of every number and quoted word is on an `ext:` line (read from the deposited page image of an official instrument) or a `src:` line (the deposited excerpt of the consolidation). The modules type the numbers of sections in Latin letters (tools/translit.py checks the Latin against the Hebrew, line by line): a Hebrew letter alef, bet, gimel or dalet after a digit is A, B, C or D (79 bet is 79B); a letter alef to he alone in brackets is (a) to (e); a letter in brackets followed by a digit is (a1) to (e1) (the bracket bet 1 is (b1)).
-- Hebrew is typed in code only where the very same words are on a quotation line (tools/hebcheck.py checks that).
-- THE NAMES BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's. NOTHING is the answer where a page prints nothing: it is a value, not an absence.
-- An instrument is typed as Printed: the row says what a page prints and when its issue is dated, and nothing about any other status.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `The status of an instrument as the row types it` IS ONE OF
    Printed

DECLARE `A column of a comparison table` IS ONE OF
    `the column headed for the previous section`
    `the column headed for the new section`

DECLARE `How a limb was read` IS ONE OF
    `official page images`
    `official page images, with the completeness of the list of instruments resting on the consolidation's header box (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`

-- An instrument as its footer prints it. `the issue date its footer prints` is the date of the issue, never a day of effect; NOTHING where the footer prints none.
DECLARE `An instrument` HAS
    `its citation` IS A STRING
    `what it is, in a working translation` IS A STRING
    `its title as the page prints it` IS A STRING
    `its footer as the page prints it` IS A STRING
    `the issue date its footer prints` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `its status as the row types it` IS A `The status of an instrument as the row types it`
    `the printed pages deposited` IS A LIST OF NUMBER

-- A subsection of a section, by the letter the page prints before it (the letter typed in Latin) and its words without the letter.
DECLARE `A lettered subsection` HAS
    `its letter, with letters in Latin` IS A STRING
    `its words` IS A STRING

-- A section as a page prints it. A section that prints lettered subsections carries them in the list, and NOTHING in `its words where it prints no lettered subsection`.
DECLARE `A section as printed` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `its number, with letters in Latin` IS A STRING
    `its margin note as the page prints it` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `the bracketed reference the page prints under the margin note` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `its words where it prints no lettered subsection` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `its lettered subsections` IS A LIST OF `A lettered subsection`

-- A definition as a page prints it: the line, and the term it defines.
DECLARE `A definition as printed` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `the term it defines` IS A STRING
    `the line as printed` IS A STRING

-- An instruction of an amending instrument: the section of the instrument that carries it, the law and the sections it names, and the words it prints.
-- `the law it names` is the words the page prints for the law (NOTHING where the section names none).
DECLARE `An instruction` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `its section in the instrument, with letters in Latin` IS A STRING
    `its margin note as the page prints it` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `the law it names` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `the sections of that law it names, with letters in Latin` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the lettered subsections of them it names, with letters in Latin` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the words it prints` IS A STRING
    `the words it puts in place` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `the words it deletes` IS A MAYBE STRING

-- A citation of an enactment: the name of the enactment, a section number and the lettered subsections, as the citing words print them.
DECLARE `A citation of an enactment` HAS
    `the enactment as the citing words name it` IS A STRING
    `the section it cites, with letters in Latin` IS A STRING
    `the lettered subsections it cites, with letters in Latin` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the citing words` IS A STRING

-- A row of a comparison table: the number printed under the heading for the previous section and the number printed under the heading for the new section, each with letters in Latin; a word the page prints in a cell is typed as it is printed.
DECLARE `A row of a comparison table` HAS
    `the number under the heading for the previous section` IS A STRING
    `the number under the heading for the new section` IS A STRING

-- A comparison table as the row types it: the rows the deposited bands print, under the headings they print.
DECLARE `A comparison table as typed` HAS
    `the instrument` IS AN `An instrument`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `the sub-heading the page prints over it` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `the heading over the previous column` IS A STRING
    `the heading over the new column` IS A STRING
    `the rows the row types` IS A LIST OF `A row of a comparison table`

DECLARE `An item of the row` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing section` IS A `A section as printed`
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

-- ===== QUESTIONS ASKED OF THE VALUES =====

GIVEN x IS A `A lettered subsection`
GIVETH A STRING
`the letter of the subsection` MEANS x's `its letter, with letters in Latin`

GIVEN s IS A `A section as printed`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the letters of the lettered subsections of the section` MEANS map `the letter of the subsection` (s's `its lettered subsections`)

GIVEN s IS A `A section as printed`, l IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section prints a lettered subsection` MEANS elem l (`the letters of the lettered subsections of the section` s)

GIVEN l IS A STRING, xs IS A LIST OF `A lettered subsection`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the words of the first subsection in the list with the letter` MEANS
    CONSIDER xs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF (x's `its letter, with letters in Latin`) EQUALS l
        THEN JUST (x's `its words`)
        ELSE `the words of the first subsection in the list with the letter` l rest

GIVEN s IS A `A section as printed`, l IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the words of the lettered subsection of the section` MEANS `the words of the first subsection in the list with the letter` l (s's `its lettered subsections`)

GIVEN s IS A `A section as printed`, l IS A STRING, w IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the lettered subsection of the section has the words in it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the words of the lettered subsection of the section` s l
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST t THEN CONTAINS t w

GIVEN s IS A `A section as printed`, w IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section without lettered subsections has the words in it` MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `its words where it prints no lettered subsection`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST t THEN CONTAINS t w

GIVEN s IS A `A section as printed`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the bracketed reference of the section` MEANS s's `the bracketed reference the page prints under the margin note`

GIVEN r IS A `A row of a comparison table`
GIVETH A STRING
`the previous number of the row` MEANS r's `the number under the heading for the previous section`

GIVEN r IS A `A row of a comparison table`
GIVETH A STRING
`the new number of the row` MEANS r's `the number under the heading for the new section`

GIVEN t IS A `A comparison table as typed`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the numbers the table types under the heading for the previous section` MEANS map `the previous number of the row` (t's `the rows the row types`)

GIVEN t IS A `A comparison table as typed`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the numbers the table types under the heading for the new section` MEANS map `the new number of the row` (t's `the rows the row types`)

-- The question the red assertions ask: does the number appear under the heading for the new section (or the previous one) in the rows this table types?
GIVEN t IS A `A comparison table as typed`, c IS A `A column of a comparison table`, n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the number appears under the column` MEANS
    IF c EQUALS `the column headed for the new section`
    THEN elem n (`the numbers the table types under the heading for the new section` t)
    ELSE elem n (`the numbers the table types under the heading for the previous section` t)

GIVEN n IS A STRING, rs IS A LIST OF `A row of a comparison table`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the new number paired with the previous number in the rows` MEANS
    CONSIDER rs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF (r's `the number under the heading for the previous section`) EQUALS n
        THEN JUST (r's `the number under the heading for the new section`)
        ELSE `the new number paired with the previous number in the rows` n rest

GIVEN t IS A `A comparison table as typed`, n IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the new number the table prints beside the previous number` MEANS `the new number paired with the previous number in the rows` n (t's `the rows the row types`)

-- A pair is on one row: the previous number and the new number are printed on the same row.
GIVEN t IS A `A comparison table as typed`, p IS A STRING, n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the table types a row with the previous number and the new number` MEANS
    `the new number the table prints beside the previous number` t p EQUALS JUST n

-- The two tables chain when the new number printed beside a previous number in the first is a previous number printed in the second.
GIVEN a IS A `A comparison table as typed`, p IS A STRING, b IS A `A comparison table as typed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the new number of the first table is a previous number of the second` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the new number the table prints beside the previous number` a p
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST n THEN `the number appears under the column` b `the column headed for the previous section` n

-- Does an instruction name the section of the Arbitration Law, where `the law it names` is the title the first page of Sefer HaChukim 535 prints?
GIVEN i IS AN `An instruction`, title IS A STRING, n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instruction names the section of the law` MEANS
    ((i's `the law it names`) EQUALS JUST title) AND (elem n (i's `the sections of that law it names, with letters in Latin`))

GIVEN title IS A STRING, n IS A STRING, xs IS A LIST OF `An instruction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some instruction in the list names the section of the law` MEANS
    CONSIDER xs
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN i FOLLOWED BY rest THEN (`the instruction names the section of the law` i title n) OR (`some instruction in the list names the section of the law` title n rest)

GIVEN i IS AN `An instruction`, title IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instruction names the law` MEANS (i's `the law it names`) EQUALS JUST title

GIVEN i IS AN `An instruction`, n IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instruction names the section number in whatever law it names` MEANS elem n (i's `the sections of that law it names, with letters in Latin`)

GIVEN c IS A `A citation of an enactment`, l IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the citation cites the lettered subsection` MEANS elem l (c's `the lettered subsections it cites, with letters in Latin`)

-- Dates: the footer's issue date, where it prints one.
GIVEN i IS AN `An instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the issue date of the instrument` MEANS i's `the issue date its footer prints`

-- The first instrument's footer prints an issue date earlier than the second's; FALSE where either footer prints none.
GIVEN a IS AN `An instrument`, b IS AN `An instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the footer of the first instrument prints an earlier issue date than the footer of the second` MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `the issue date its footer prints`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER b's `the issue date its footer prints`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST y THEN x LESS THAN y
